NAME
       whatis - show the one-line description of manual pages

SYNOPSIS
       whatis NAME...

DESCRIPTION
       whatis looks NAME up in the manual page index and prints the NAME line
       of every page with exactly that name, with its section number:
       passwd (1) for the command, passwd (5) for the file format. It is the
       same as man -f. To search descriptions for a word, use apropos (man
       -k) instead.

       If whatis or apropos find nothing on a fresh system, the index may not
       have been built yet; run mandb as root.

EXAMPLES
           whatis passwd

SEE ALSO
       apropos(1), man(1), mandb(8)
